{"parentUuid":"0232cd23-f665-427e-9fa7-f1bbf8308ba9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FRFqHNtGhYbNA9D5P9ioma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NTgt5Qzf3ax11stad9XBAx","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"Hexaly\" OR \"LocalSolver\" version 13 release notes 2025 2026"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7474,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7474,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxmZ1R5S65bSqtpKAgX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"91db5008-f891-4bed-b97f-cc970524c1b1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:49.136Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"56e95e81-788b-4897-a791-67e9544fb94a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H84gZYVW3Gm3igH1fsHtY9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hexaly optimizer academic license application 2026 free\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Download\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/download\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly Optimizer\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/hexaly-optimizer\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Installation on Windows — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/installation/installationonwindows.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly Optimizer 14.5\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/announcements/hexaly-optimizer-14-5\"},{\"title\":\"Installation on macOS — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/installation/installationonmacosx.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPLEX vs. Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/cplex\"},{\"title\":\"Simulation Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/simulation-optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi vs. Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/gurobi\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Hexaly Optimizer academic licenses for 2026:\n\n## Academic License Information\n\nAcademic licenses are FREE for educational and fundamental research purposes. Hexaly offers 3-month licenses for free, renewable forever, to individual students. You have full access to Hexaly Optimizer and Hexaly Studio to solve problems and build optimization apps for FREE.\n\n## How to Apply\n\nTo obtain an academic license, you can go to the Hexaly website to register and request a free academic license. Note that licenses are manually delivered by a member of the Hexaly team, so the whole procedure can take a few days.\n\n## Additional Options\n\nIf you prefer not to wait for an academic license, you can discover the ease of use and performance of Hexaly through a free 1-month trial, or enjoy free academic access.\n\nThe pricing and download pages on the Hexaly website are current as of February 2026, confirming that these free academic license offerings remain available.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"84fe56bf-e4dd-47bb-93ae-b6edf63f9c12","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:53.273Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"56e95e81-788b-4897-a791-67e9544fb94a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0232cd23-f665-427e-9fa7-f1bbf8308ba9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QrAQZiWA8oHxc48Su1oywd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hexaly vs Gurobi benchmark large scale MILP 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Gurobi vs. Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/gurobi\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly vs Gurobi on the Bin Packing Problem (BPP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-gurobi-bin-packing-problem\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly, Gurobi, OR-Tools, OptaPlanner, jsprit on the Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem (CVRP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-gurobi-capacitated-vehicle-routing-problem-cvrp\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly, Gurobi, OR-Tools on the Resource-Constrained Project Scheduling Problem (RCPSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-or-tools-on-the-resource-constrained-project-scheduling-problem-rcpsp\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly vs Gurobi on the Flexible Job Shop Scheduling Problem (FJSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-gurobi-flexible-job-shop-scheduling-problem-fjsp\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly on very large-scale instances of the Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem (CVRP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/large-scale-instances-capacitated-vehicle-routing-problem-cvrp\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly, CP Optimizer, OR-Tools, Gurobi, Cplex on very large-scale instances of the Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-cp-optimizer-vs-or-tools-on-the-job-shop-scheduling-problem-jssp\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly vs Gurobi on the Traveling Salesman Problem (TSP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-gurobi-traveling-salesman-problem-tsp\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly, Gurobi, OR-Tools on the Team Orienteering Problem (TOP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-gurobi-or-tools-team-orienteering-problem-top\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly vs Gurobi on the Car Sequencing Problem with Paint-Shop Batching Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/benchmarks/hexaly-vs-gurobi-on-the-car-sequencing-problem-with-paint-shop-batching-constraints\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about benchmarks comparing Hexaly and Gurobi on large-scale optimization problems:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nHexaly is not a MILP solver but rather a global optimization solver, while Gurobi is a Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) solver. This fundamental difference makes direct comparisons context-dependent.\n\n### Recent Benchmarks (2025-2026)\n\nHexaly has published multiple recent benchmarks comparing its performance to Gurobi on large-scale problems:\n\n**Bin Packing Problem:** After 1 minute, the worst gap observed for Hexaly over 240 instances is 0.3%, while Gurobi's average gap is 44%.\n\n**Traveling Salesman Problem:** Hexaly finds near-optimal solutions for instances with 10,000 cities, whereas Gurobi fails to find quality solutions for instances with more than 300 cities.\n\n**Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem:** Gurobi fails to find decent solutions in 1 minute of running time, even for small-sized instances.\n\n**Job Shop Scheduling:** OR-Tools, Gurobi, and Cplex fail to deliver feasible solutions within 6 hours of running time on very large-scale instances.\n\n### Important Context\n\nHexaly doesn't claim to outperform Gurobi on all problems, having chosen problems related to Supply Chain and Workforce Management. Additionally, new benchmarks will be published in the coming months related to different business domains.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"de97c849-6870-4837-9810-6dc0cd0f26a0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:54.878Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0232cd23-f665-427e-9fa7-f1bbf8308ba9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"91db5008-f891-4bed-b97f-cc970524c1b1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NTgt5Qzf3ax11stad9XBAx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Hexaly\" OR \"LocalSolver\" version 13 release notes 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Migrate from LocalSolver to Hexaly — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/migration.html\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver 6.5 — Hexaly 13.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/localsolver65.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver 8.0 — Hexaly 13.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/localsolver80.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"Changelog — Hexaly 13.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Changelog — Hexaly 14.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/index.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver 10.5 — Hexaly 13.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/localsolver105.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"New release: LocalSolver 12.0\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/announcement/new-release-localsolver-12-0\"},{\"title\":\"Localsolver: Package localsolver\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/6_0/csharp/namespacelocalsolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly 11.5\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/announcements/new-release-localsolver-11-5\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver 7.0 — Hexaly 13.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/localsolver70.html?redirect\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Hexaly/LocalSolver version releases. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Version 13 Release Information\n\nHexaly 13.0 was released in July 2024, marking a significant migration milestone. The old APIs are still supported, but no new features will be added, allowing you to benefit from the latest performance enhancements and bug fixes without changing your code.\n\n## Recent Releases (2025-2026)\n\nThe search results indicate that more recent versions have been released:\n\n- Hexaly 14.0 is planned for mid-2025, with the old LocalSolver APIs disappearing completely and the transition to Hexaly being complete.\n\n- LocalSolver 12.0 (released January 2025) includes new features and performance improvements on Routing, Scheduling, Packing, and more, including a new Geodata module for fast computation of distance and time matrices.\n\n- Hexaly 11.5 (released September 2025) found optimal solutions in less than 1 minute for 734 instances over 1,668 in the MINLPLib benchmark.\n\nFor detailed release notes, you can visit the official Hexaly documentation changelog at https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/changelog/index.html\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"86f4ede0-bd03-4b6a-91e0-65d228bc9ab6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:55.740Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"91db5008-f891-4bed-b97f-cc970524c1b1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"054832a6-5a53-4082-b3f0-f6717b095ada","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XiKY16ozWEQBaqwmLhcfyf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hexaly Python API tutorial facility location placement example\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Facility Location (FLP) — Hexaly 13.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/exampletour/facilitylocation.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"Facility Location Problem (FLP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/templates/facility-location-problem-flp\"},{\"title\":\"Python API Reference — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/pythonapi/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Capacitated Facility Location Problem (CFLP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/templates/capacitated-facility-location-problem-cflp\"},{\"title\":\"Capacitated Facility Location (CFLP) — Hexaly 13.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/exampletour/capacitated-facility-location-problem-cflp.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"Capacitated Facility Location (CFLP) — Hexaly 13.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/exampletour/capacitated-facility-location-problem-cflp.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - nextmv-io/community-apps: Pre-built decision models serving as the base for Marketplace subscription apps. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nextmv-io/community-apps\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly Modeler — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/pythonapi/modeler/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly · Nextmv Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.nextmv.io/docs/integrations/solvers/hexaly\"},{\"title\":\"Quick Start in Python — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/quickstart/quickstartpython/index.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the Hexaly Python API tutorial for facility location placement problems.\n\n## Facility Location Problem Overview\n\nThe facility location problem is defined as follows: given a set of N locations and a transportation cost W between each pair of locations, select a subset S of p locations, which become facilities, in order to minimize transportation costs. The transportation cost for a location is defined as the distance to the closest facility, that is, the closest location in S. Thus, it aims to provide an optimal placement of facilities to minimize transportation costs.\n\n## Python API Implementation\n\nThe Python implementation reads instance data, defines optimization model with boolean decision variables for each location (1 if facility, 0 otherwise), and ensures no more than p locations are selected as facilities.\n\nThe key steps in the Python API approach include:\n\n1. **Reading Instance Data**: Loading the number of locations (N), number of facilities to select (p), weight matrix of shortest paths between locations (w), and maximum distance (wmax).\n\n2. **Model Declaration**: Creating boolean decision variables for each location and constraints to limit the number of facilities.\n\n3. **Cost Computation**: The transportation cost between each location i and the closest facility in S is represented by cost[i]: it is the minimum value among costs[i][j] for all j. The objective is then to minimize the sum of these transportation costs.\n\n## Available Examples\n\nThe data files pmed1.in, pmed2.in, …, pmed40.in provided come from the OR-LIB. They are the 40 test problems from Table 2 of J.E.Beasley \"A note on solving large p-median problems\" European Journal of Operational Research 21 (1985) 270-273.\n\nThe official Hexaly documentation provides complete working examples with both the HXM modeling language and Python API implementations that you can reference directly at their documentation website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"15adcee0-8963-4ad0-b3f4-d775422fc9a5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:56.487Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"054832a6-5a53-4082-b3f0-f6717b095ada","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
