{"parentUuid":"09d7cdc3-59c0-4cf8-ac2d-3e4f3cb5a621","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GEaJSbVh164UE8dEjgMsYg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SPKJB9Ht6wUXe1A6MbtLS5","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/exampletour/capacitated-facility-location-problem-cflp.html","prompt":"Extract the Python model code for capacitated facility location: variable declarations (bool, int, set), constraints (sum, eq, ge), objective. Show actual API methods like model.bool(), model.sum(), model.constraint(), etc."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2484,"cache_read_input_tokens":20595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2484,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":58,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxnYnoFVefqyxdgmAFH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e2427e70-eec5-4951-81c6-30b61e51b433","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:07.835Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e104b8f7-b5dd-4b49-9624-0b156a037259","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G7B3qRi5hULVWM8SLwEkmS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Hexaly Academic License Details\n\n**Eligibility:**\nStudents and educators/researchers at schools and universities qualify for free academic licenses for \"educational and fundamental research purposes.\"\n\n**Duration & Renewal:**\n- Individual students: \"3-month licenses for free, renewable forever\"\n- Institutional (schools/universities): \"FREE annual unlimited academic licenses\"\n\n**What's Included:**\nFull access to Hexaly Optimizer and Hexaly Studio, plus:\n- 2 new releases each year\n- Dedicated and responsive support\n- Exclusive training sessions\n\n**Restrictions & Limits:**\nThe page does not specify restrictions on problem size or explicit commercial use prohibitions. However, licenses are limited to \"educational and fundamental research purposes.\"\n\n**Application URL:**\nRegistration begins at https://www.hexaly.com/registration\n\nFor institutional licenses, prospective users should \"Contact us\" at https://www.hexaly.com/contact-us\n\n**Note:**\nThe content does not detail specific technical limitations or commercial use restrictions beyond the stated educational/research scope."}]},"uuid":"cf07b77c-5dcc-471c-a014-064e40d6f5d2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:08.406Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e104b8f7-b5dd-4b49-9624-0b156a037259","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cf07b77c-5dcc-471c-a014-064e40d6f5d2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GEaJSbVh164UE8dEjgMsYg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JxCzWRVHy3C3FuV3dLFJ5y","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/pythonapi/index.html","prompt":"List the main Python API objects: HexalyOptimizer, Model, Solution, Param. List operator methods on Model (bool, int, float, set, list, sum, prod, eq, geq, leq, count, contains, at, partition, disjoint, etc). List Param controls (timeLimit, nbThreads, seed, verbosity, iterationLimit)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2484,"cache_read_input_tokens":20595,"output_tokens":705,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2484},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2664,"output_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":20595,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2484,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxnYnoFVefqyxdgmAFH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"62935837-1ef8-4d85-8be4-60aa5b879cf9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:10.361Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"09d7cdc3-59c0-4cf8-ac2d-3e4f3cb5a621","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NmSMgg3ZsQPHq3FMY9zFZS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Hexaly Optimizer Python Quick Start\n\nBased on the documentation, here's what a basic Python example would involve:\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Imports and Setup:**\nThe documentation indicates you'd import from `hexaly.optimizer` module after installing via:\n```\npip install hexaly -i https://pip.hexaly.com\n```\n\n**Model Creation:**\nYou instantiate an optimizer and create a model through its API, similar to how other solvers structure object-oriented interfaces.\n\n**Decision Variables:**\nThe framework supports multiple variable types:\n- Boolean decisions\n- Floating-point decisions  \n- Integer decisions\n- Set and list decisions\n- Interval decisions\n\n**Constraints and Objectives:**\nThe platform uses \"constraint\" and \"minimize/maximize\" statements to define the problem structure.\n\n**Solving:**\nThe documentation notes that \"having instantiated the model, no additional code has to be written in order to run the solver\" - suggesting a straightforward solve invocation.\n\n**Parameters:**\nConfiguration options include:\n- Time limits\n- Thread count\n- Random seed\n- Display settings for objectives and violated constraints\n- Warning levels\n\n## Documentation Path\n\nFor complete working examples, the docs reference sections on \"Solving Your First Model in Python\" and \"Solving Your First Business Problem in Python\" with full code samples, though the actual example code isn't included in the provided content extract."}]},"uuid":"2e4e8d23-f442-4812-b64d-e89901961d51","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:11.471Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"09d7cdc3-59c0-4cf8-ac2d-3e4f3cb5a621","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e2427e70-eec5-4951-81c6-30b61e51b433","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPKJB9Ht6wUXe1A6MbtLS5","type":"tool_result","content":"# Python Model Code for Capacitated Facility Location\n\nBased on the Hexaly documentation, here are the key Python API methods used in the CFLP model:\n\n## Variable Declarations\n\n```python\n# Set variables representing sites assigned to each facility\nfacility_assignments = [model.set(nb_sites) for _ in range(nb_max_facilities)]\n```\n\nThe `model.set()` method creates decision variables that are collections of sites.\n\n## Constraints\n\n```python\n# Partition constraint ensures each site assigned to exactly one facility\nmodel.constraint(model.partition(facility_assignments))\n\n# Capacity constraint using lambda functions\ndemand_lambda = model.lambda_function(lambda i: demand[i])\nmodel.constraint(model.sum(facility, demand_lambda) <= capacity_data[f])\n```\n\nKey constraint methods:\n- `model.partition()` - enforces that sets partition the domain\n- `model.constraint()` - adds a constraint to the model\n- `model.sum()` - aggregates values, accepting lambda functions for dynamic computation\n\n## Objective Function\n\n```python\n# Cost calculation with conditional opening price\ncostSelector = model.lambda_function(lambda i: model.at(allocation_price, f, i))\ncost[f] = model.sum(facility, costSelector) + opening_price_data[f] * (size > 0)\n\n# Minimize total cost\ntotalCost = model.sum(cost)\nmodel.minimize(totalCost)\n```\n\nThe model uses `model.minimize()` to define the objective and leverages `model.at()` for array indexing within lambda expressions."}]},"uuid":"701c8824-918f-4ff5-913b-67b8f4ae5f4b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:13.389Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2427e70-eec5-4951-81c6-30b61e51b433","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"62935837-1ef8-4d85-8be4-60aa5b879cf9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"aef4c071a06991685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JxCzWRVHy3C3FuV3dLFJ5y","type":"tool_result","content":"# Hexaly Python API Overview\n\n## Main Python API Objects\n\nThe core components of Hexaly's Python API include:\n\n1. **HexalyOptimizer** - The primary solver class for creating and executing optimization models\n2. **HxModel** - Container for decision variables, constraints, and objectives\n3. **HxSolution** - Represents the optimization result with status and variable values\n4. **HxParam** - Configuration object for controlling solver behavior\n\n## Model Operator Methods\n\nThe HxModel class provides numerous mathematical operators for building expressions:\n\n- **Numeric operators**: `sum()`, `prod()` (product)\n- **Comparison operators**: `eq()` (equality), `geq()` (greater-or-equal), `leq()` (less-or-equal)\n- **Collection operators**: `count()`, `contains()`, `partition()`, `disjoint()`\n- **Data access**: `at()` (array indexing)\n- **Type-specific**: `bool`, `int`, `float`, `set`, `list` decision variables\n\n## Parameter Controls (HxParam)\n\nKey solver configuration parameters include:\n\n- **timeLimit** - Maximum solving duration\n- **nbThreads** - Number of parallel threads\n- **seed** - Random number generator seed\n- **verbosity** - Output detail level\n- **iterationLimit** - Maximum iteration count\n\nThese parameters allow fine-tuning solver performance and behavior for different optimization scenarios."}]},"uuid":"eadf49da-8feb-4503-9933-def969775629","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:14.688Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"62935837-1ef8-4d85-8be4-60aa5b879cf9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
